<title>USA: KEDO buys July fuel oil from BP, Petro Diamond.</title>
<headline>KEDO buys July fuel oil from BP, Petro Diamond.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korean Peninsula Energy Development Organization (KEDO) Monday bought 36,000 metric tonnes of heavy fuel oil from British Petroleum's BP Singapore Pte Ltd and up to 24,000 tonnes from Mitsubishi Corp's Petro Diamond Co Ltd for July delivery.</p>
<p>BP sold the oil for $120.90 per tonne for delivery to Sonbong, North Korea in one cargo during July 21-30.</p>
<p>Petro Diamond sold 22,000 to 24,000 tonnes loading in Aichi, Japan during July 15-19 at $109.75 per tonne, with freight to Nampo and Songrim, North Korea, at $18.75 per tonne.  </p>
<p>KEDO, an organization created to ensure that North Korea freezes its nuclear weapons program, has agreed to supply the country with 500,000 tonnes of fuel oil annually.</p>
</text>
